  {
    "episode_id": 44925,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44925.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm telling you, it's an amazing situation that you have when a Congress congressional office turns over and folks don't understand how many staffers and how much. It's not just a policy thing. It's a personal service thing and that you and Jodi Heis specifically work so well together to retain as many of your key people as you possibly could hats off to all of you. And by the way, this cuts across the board. I'd give praise to the Democrats that have done the same thing. Often a big shake up for unnecessary reasons when a person retires or moves on and those staffers, you lose an awful lot of very, very wise folks and experienced people if you let them get away from you. And I just wanted to praise you for keeping those folks around. You've done a",
