    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 44925,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/4/44925.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "We'll drop that building a hopper first thing in the morning, and then hopefully get that thing passed through the house in short order. And you know you're right, it's a sad day in this country when we have let our southern border down there just be invaded by, you know, over 8 million people, almost 2 million people that got away that we don't know who in the world they are, what they came in for, what they're doing while they're here. And then over 300 that we have called, they were on the terrorist list. And that in itself should identify a problem. We have a process and we have ports of entry that people need to come through. But they apparently don't feel like they have to do that. And now we have a Biden administration that feels the same way that they don't have to do that. So when the state of Texas decides that they're going to take matters into their own hand to protect the people of the state of Texas, that the Supreme Court sides with the Biden administration and the way that they have There is one main thing that Congress can do. And as you well know, we have the power of the purse. And therefore, we just need to defund that so that the federal government cannot enforce it by paying for it. And that is to touch or take down any of this razor wire.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "We will remove the building at the border first thing in the morning.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "There exists a formal immigration process requiring legal port-of-entry procedures.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "It is a sad day in the country due to lax control of the southern border.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "More than 300 individuals among them are listed on a terrorist watchlist.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The goal is to quickly pass the removed structure through the house.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Texas has taken unilateral action to secure its borders against federal inaction.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "Over 8 million people have entered the U.S. illegally without being accounted for.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Nearly 2 million of those individuals remain unidentified and untracked.",
